===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Lacking or being without [[air]].
# Lacking air circulation.
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=7|passage={{...}} St. Bede's at this period of its history was perhaps the poorest and most miserable parish in the East End of London. Close-packed, crushed by the buttressed height of the railway viaduct, rendered '''airless''' by huge walls of factories, it at once banished lively interest from a stranger's mind and left only a dull oppression of the spirit.}}
# With air that is [[stale]].
# {{lb|en|medical}} Suffering from [[asphyxia]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[stifling|Stifling]]; [[dead]]; lacking vitality or excitement.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 8 2012|author=Scott Tobias|title=''Memento''’s puzzle structure hides big twists and bigger profundities|newspaper=The AV Club|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/mementos-puzzle-structure-obscures-its-humor-and-i,88452/
|passage=The worst that can—and has—been said about Memento is that it’s an '''airless''' gimmick, visually undistinguished, and not even all that sophisticated when the puzzle pieces are finally put together.}}

